  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors: the vector between two points</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.2: Write the vector AB from the coordinates of A and B, and find a point from a starting point and a vector.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question B5(a) in Section B of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: new numbers, Kenyan context, STACK randomisation, a point found from a vector added, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
